manage.js starts a configurable fleet of the clients that sit in the folders below it.
A configurable number of readers, writers and reader_writers, plus a single stats server.
Readers and writers are headless, so only the stats server and the reader_writers get ports.
It has no dependencies of its own and runs pnpm install for any client that has never been installed.
Each client keeps its own stdout, prefixed with its label, and ctrl-c stops the whole fleet.

  node manage.js --readers 2 --writers 3 --reader-writers 1
  node manage.js --help
